## #03 — One complete byte-preserving flow
Explicit fixture setup stands a disposable context, external Clerk store, declared
instruction/claim/link, pre-reserved book member and the accepted protocol worker.
Run delivery through the accepted seam, allowing one real protocol-worker subprocess.
Collect to Clerk, then invoke the accepted handoff against that returned job.
No fabrication of an unrelated post-return report. The existing worker's result.json
artifact may be explicitly designated the SYNTHETIC final-report payload for this
protocol proof; preserve its bytes as such and do not claim it is a narrative builder
report or semantic review. Transport envelope/evidence stays distinct from that file.
Record delivery/request/result/Clerk event/claim/source/report/member/reservation/
receipt/handoff identities and raw outputs. Verify report and payload bytes through
accepted tools and direct byte comparison, not another receipt validator.
The work_ref and fixture routing labels are explicit supplied labels, not authority.
No live queue, job, role, registry, canonical assignment or batch-pointer mutation.

## #04 — Repetition and partial proof
Repeat the same delivery/handoff on the same disposable fixture. Show exactly one
worker launch, one Clerk returned event and one complete capture/handoff record;
the identical repetition changes no durable source/job/member/record bytes. This is
a bounded fixture observation, not a general exactly-once guarantee. Changed payload/
event/binding must refuse and not launch another worker or replace the capture.
Include a non-collected/failed worker case with no capture, and a stop after capture
before completed handoff: files retained, current custody separate from handoff
completion, next repetition attention rather than auto-resume. Use accepted private
in-process seams for fault tests, not new runtime fault switches. Unknown pin/timeout/
inspection outcomes remain unknown. Any recovery or new submission is outside scope.

## #05 — Evidence and return
Provide exact source-view manifest, fixture requests and full raw outputs in the
flow05.19 evidence directory. results.json must embed or exactly index retained
raw bytes/hashes (not point only at deleted temporary files), the byte comparisons,
launch/event counts, before/after trees and case results. Clearly label fixture acts
and unknowns. Tests cover malformed inputs/unsafe paths/failed pins before execution,
normal complete flow, read-only repetition, changed binding/payload, failed delivery
and post-capture stop. No unchanged full core suites. Show source/Git/other-worker
immutability. Any cleanup must verify owned absolute temporary roots and remove only
those roots; no broad temp sweep or cross-shell deletion.
Retain first failures/reruns and commands/exits/skips in tests.txt/verification.json;
fully reread/disposition notes. README explains what compute now does end-to-end,
what Prime still decides, and one smallest next integration recommendation. No
new authority, app wiring or production claims. Only new lab,06.19,flow05.19 evidence
and named return may change. Capture/freshly verify; no shared Git commits/pushes.
